.TH LIBRDP-COCOA-VIEWER 1 "2026-07-15" "librdp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-cocoa-viewer \- native macOS RDP client viewer for librdp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-cocoa-viewer
.B --target
.I host
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-cocoa-viewer
is the native Cocoa frontend for exercising the public librdp client APIs on macOS. It uses AppKit and CoreGraphics for windowing, framebuffer presentation, input, cursor updates, clipboard access, and certificate prompts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --target " host"
Remote host name or address.
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Remote TCP port. The default is 3389.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
User name for authentication.
.TP
.BI --password " value"
Password for authentication. Avoid placing credentials in shell history on shared systems.
.TP
.BI --domain " name"
Authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --width " px"
Initial desktop width.
.TP
.BI --height " px"
Initial desktop height.
.TP
.BI --security " auto|rdp|tls|nla"
Security negotiation mode.
.TP
.B --tls-prompt-cert
Print the presented TLS certificate and ask whether to trust it for the current connection.
.TP
.B --tls-accept-any-cert
Accept the presented TLS certificate for the current connection without prompting after printing certificate details.
.TP
.B --accept-tls-certificate
Compatibility alias for
.BR --tls-accept-any-cert .
.TP
.BI --rail " app=program"
Request a RemoteApp launch for the selected program.
.TP
.BI --drive " name=path"
Redirect a filesystem drive through the public device redirection settings.
.TP
.BI --serial " name=path"
Redirect a serial port selector.
.TP
.BI --parallel " name=path"
Redirect a parallel port selector.
.TP
.BI --printer " name=driver=path"
Configure a redirected printer.
.TP
.BI --audio-output " [device=name]"
Enable audio output redirection and select the Core Audio device selector used by the viewer configuration.
.TP
.BI --audio-input " [device=name]"
Enable audio input redirection and select the Core Audio device selector used by the viewer configuration.
.TP
.BI --video " file=path"
Enable video output capture into a file sink.
.TP
.BI --camera " file=path"
Enable camera redirection with a bounded file source for deterministic capture paths.
.TP
.BI --smartcard " [pcsc|source]"
Enable smartcard redirection with a PC/SC or explicit source selector.
.TP
.BI --usb " vid:pid|bus:dev"
Enable USB redirection for the selected device.
.TP
.B --pnp
Enable PnP device metadata redirection.
.TP
.BI --webauthn " [fido2|mock|provider]"
Enable WebAuthn redirection with the selected provider.
.TP
.BI --webauthn-rp-id " id"
Allow one WebAuthn relying-party identifier.
.TP
.B --cr2
Enable composited-remoting configuration.
.TP
.B --echo
Enable the echo diagnostics channel.
.TP
.B --telemetry
Enable telemetry configuration.
.TP
.B --multitransport
Enable multitransport negotiation.
.TP
.BI --gateway " url"
Tunnel the RDP connection through an HTTP CONNECT or Microsoft RD Gateway endpoint.
.TP
.BI --gateway-mode " http-connect|rdg-http"
Gateway transport mode. The default is http-connect.
.TP
.BI --gateway-user " name"
Gateway user name. Session credentials are reused when gateway credentials are omitted.
.TP
.BI --gateway-password " value"
Gateway password.
.TP
.BI --gateway-domain " name"
Gateway authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --gateway-timeout " ms"
Gateway operation timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.B --gateway-no-session-credentials
Do not reuse session credentials for gateway authentication.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT
Enable client, viewer, surface, input, channel, audio, video, and backend trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_TRANSPORT
Enable TCP, TLS, read, write, wait, timeout, and close trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL
Enable handshake, parser, PDU, capability, slow-path, fast-path, channel, and codec trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_LEVEL
Set trace verbosity: error, warn, info, debug, trace, or the numeric values 0 through 4.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_HEX_BYTES
Set the maximum number of bytes emitted by bounded protocol hexdumps.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
librdp-cocoa-viewer --target host --user user --password password --security nla

LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT=1 LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL=1 librdp-cocoa-viewer --target host --security nla
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp (7),
.BR librdp-api (7),
.BR librdp-tracing (7)
